    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for marinated pork souvlaki that a Greek place would charge you a lunch special price for, with less meat.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003ePork tenderloin is the tender cut that goes on sale constantly.\u003c/strong\u003e Watch for it, buy two, and freeze one. It thaws overnight and marinates while it does.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eThe marinade is nearly free.\u003c/strong\u003e Vinegar, lemon juice, garlic, mustard, and dried oregano are all pantry items, and the olive oil is the only meaningful cost in it.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eGive it time, not more ingredients.\u003c/strong\u003e Marinating overnight costs nothing and does more for the flavor than anything you could add to the bowl.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eRed onion roasts right alongside the pork.\u003c/strong\u003e One sheet pan, two components, and the onion picks up the marinade drippings for free."
